# W185 ZADIG-HELP: Anleitung "Original-Controller anschliessen" als lokales HTML
gui.zadig_btn=Setup guide
gui.zadig_title=Connect the original controller
gui.zadig_need_h=What you need
gui.zadig_need=Original Steel Battalion controller\nXbox-male → USB-A-female adapter (standard part, no cable cutting)\nFree USB port directly on the PC (no hub, 500 mA bus-powered)
gui.zadig_driver_h=One-time driver setup with Zadig
gui.zadig_driver=Download Zadig from its official site and start it: https://zadig.akeo.ie/\nIn Zadig: Options → List All Devices\nSelect the device 0A7B:D000 (often "Unknown Device #1")\nDriver target: WinUSB → Install Driver
gui.zadig_warn=Warning: only ever select the device 0A7B:D000 – never your keyboard, mouse, headset or webcam. Check the ID twice before installing.
gui.zadig_admin=Admin rights are needed once for this step only. The binding lives on your PC; the controller still works on the original Xbox.
gui.zadig_launch_h=In the launcher
gui.zadig_launch=On the Controls page, turn on "Original controller (USB)"\nPress Check\nThe status must read "Device found"
gui.zadig_assist_h=Test & calibrate
gui.zadig_assist=Open "Test & calibrate..." on the Controls page\nLive: every button, axis, tuner notch and gear position must react\nGuided test: press everything once in order\nCalibrate: measures rest, ends and deadzone of the spring-loaded axes and pedals
gui.zadig_center=Aiming lever, gear lever and tuner do not center themselves: they stay where you leave them, so there is no center calibration for them. When the game starts, do not touch the pedals or the rotation and sight axes (rest is captured automatically).
gui.zadig_start_h=Start the mech
gui.zadig_start=Close the cockpit hatch\nIgnition on (the OS boots)\nOn the status check screen only: flip all five toggle switches (only OFF→ON counts)\nSTART once every bar is above the line\nLamp test: "Test & calibrate..." → Lamps (all 37 lamps in order)
gui.zadig_fix_h=Troubleshooting
